# Shared start of LAR, LSL, VERR and VERW (the decoder puts it in front of
# each). None of them faults on a bad selector: a null selector or one past
# its table's limit is simply not found. The present bit is not checked.
# `visible` is the 386 privilege test: DPL at least CPL and RPL, or a
# conforming code segment, which is visible at any level.
require_protected_mode
$INPUT
read_descriptor raw found selector
const k32 64 32
lshr high_raw raw k32
trunc high high_raw 32
trunc low raw 32
const k8 32 8
lshr access_shifted high k8
trunc access access_shifted 8
bit segment access 4
bit code_bit access 3
bit conforming_bit access 2
bit read_write access 1
and code segment code_bit
and conforming code conforming_bit
const type_mask 8 15
and kind access type_mask
const k5 8 5
lshr dpl_shifted access k5
const m3 8 3
and dpl dpl_shifted m3
read_cpl cpl
trunc selector_low selector 8
and rpl selector_low m3
ult below_cpl dpl cpl
ult below_rpl dpl rpl
or hidden below_cpl below_rpl
not privileged hidden
or visible privileged conforming
